# Turn to Frog sets base power and toughness 1/1 in layer 7b; Giant Growth's +3/+3 modifies them in layer 7c, which
# always applies after 7b whatever the timestamps (CR 613.4b-c; Turn to Frog's ruling: "Effects that modify a creature's
# power and/or toughness ... will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect"). On turn 3 Bot1
# casts Giant Growth and then Turn to Frog at its Llanowar Elves; on turn 4 Bot2 does the same in the other order. Each
# Elves is a 4/4 blue Frog (layers 4 and 5: Frog in place of Elf Druid, blue in place of green), not a 1/1, and has lost
# its "{T}: Add {G}" (layer 6): Bot1 is not offered it (the refusal), and on turn 5, the frog gone with the cleanup of turn
# 3 (CR 514.2), it is a 1/1 green Elf Druid again and taps for {G} (the positive control).

